<h2>The Quick Answer</h2>

<p>
  Arabica and Robusta are two species of coffee plant. Arabica (<em>Coffea arabica</em>) is considered the premium variety — it has more complex flavours, less bitterness, and accounts for about 60% of world coffee production. Robusta (<em>Coffea canephora</em>) is hardier, cheaper, has more caffeine, and is used in instant coffee, espresso blends, and commercial-grade coffee.
</p>

<p>
  But it's not as simple as "Arabica = good, Robusta = bad." There's exceptional Robusta and terrible Arabica. The species is just a starting point.
</p>

<h2>Head-to-Head Comparison</h2>

